<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113733" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χελῑδ-ονίας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, a kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tunny-fish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Diph.Siph.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				8.356f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἰχθῦς</span> the more northerly fish
			of the constellation Pisces, <i><span class="en">
				Theon
			</span></i> ad <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				242
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>the spring wind, because the swallows come with it,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				7.15.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				2.122
			</span></i>.</div>
